  "goodToKnow": "Der Weinbau is wine growing or viticulture. Germany has 13 official Weinbaugebiete, including Rheinhessen (the largest), the Pfalz, Mosel and Franken, and is especially known for Riesling. Der Winzer is the winemaker, der Weinberg the vineyard, and die Weinlese the grape harvest. Many villages hold Weinfeste in late summer. It has no plural."
